content.human_approval_gates_design_and_implemen:
### Three-Tier Approval System

Drawing from the "approval tier" framework described in The Butler's guide, the architecture implements three escalation levels [human_approval_gates_design_and_implementation[0]] [24]:

| Tier | Name | Trigger | Action | Example |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Auto-approve** | Read-only operations, idempotent queries | Execute immediately, log for audit | Parallel API search, local model reasoning |
| 2 | **Notify-and-proceed** | Low-risk writes, non-destructive updates | Send notification, proceed after 15-min timeout | Append to log file, update internal state |
| 3 | **Mandatory approval** | Destructive or external-facing actions | Block until human explicitly approves | Overwrite existing file, send external API call, delete data |

### Preventing Approval Fatigue

The primary failure mode of approval systems is "users clicking approve without reading," which occurs when too many Tier-3 approvals are requested. The design mitigates this through:

- **Batching**: Group multiple proposed actions into a single approval screen showing a diff-style summary, rather than individual approvals per action.
- **Context preservation**: Each approval request includes the original query, the Parallel research summary, and the local model's reasoning chain - not just the proposed action.
- **Confidence scoring**: The local model self-rates its confidence (0-1) for each proposed action; only actions below 0.8 confidence trigger Tier-3 approval.
- **Timeout escalation**: Tier-2 approvals auto-proceed after 15 minutes; Tier-3 approvals escalate to a secondary reviewer after 1 hour [human_approval_gates_design_and_implementation[1]] [22].

### Technical Implementation in Node.js

The approval gate is implemented as a BullMQ job pause/resume pattern:

```javascript
// When job reaches approval stage
async function requestApproval(job, proposedActions) {
  await job.updateData({ ...job.data, status: 'AWAITING_APPROVAL', proposedActions });
  // Store in SQLite for persistence across restarts
  db.prepare(`UPDATE jobs SET status = ?, proposed_actions = ? WHERE id = ?`)
    .run('AWAITING_APPROVAL', JSON.stringify(proposedActions), job.id);
  // Job pauses - BullMQ will not process further until resumed
}

// Approval endpoint
app.post('/api/jobs/:id/approve', async (req, res) => {
  const job = await queue.getJob(req.params.id);
  if (!job || job.data.status !== 'AWAITING_APPROVAL') return res.status(404).send();
  // Audit log
  db.prepare(`INSERT INTO approval_audit (job_id, action, user, timestamp) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)`)
    .run(job.id, 'APPROVED', req.body.approver, new Date().toISOString());
  await job.updateData({ ...job.data, status: 'APPROVED' });
  // Resume processing
  await queue.getJob(req.params.id).promote();
  res.json({ status: 'APPROVED' });
});
```

