content.filesystem_updates_design_patterns:
### Output Directory Structure

```
./output/
  research/           # Parallel Deep Research raw results (JSON)
    2026-06-05_topic-slug.json
  reports/            # Local model-generated reports (Markdown)
    2026-06-05_topic-slug.md
  data/               # Structured data extracts (CSV/JSON)
    2026-06-05_topic-slug.csv
  logs/               # Pipeline execution logs
    2026-06-05_pipeline.log
  .manifest.json      # Index of all generated files with metadata
```

### Manifest-Based Tracking

A `.manifest.json` file tracks all outputs, enabling the dashboard to display file history without scanning the filesystem:

```javascript
{
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "research/2026-06-05_quantum-computing.json",
      "jobId": "job-uuid-123",
      "type": "research",
      "query": "latest quantum computing advances",
      "sources": 18,
      "createdAt": "2026-06-05T10:15:00Z",
      "approvedBy": "user@local"
    }
  ]
}
```

### Real-Time Dashboard Updates via File Watcher

The dashboard uses `chokidar` to watch the output directory and push changes to the UI via Server-Sent Events (SSE):

```javascript
const chokidar = require('chokidar');
const watcher = chokidar.watch('./output');

watcher.on('add', (filePath) => {
  // Notify connected dashboard clients
  sseClients.forEach(client => {
    client.write(`data: ${JSON.stringify({ event: 'file_added', path: filePath })}\n\n`);
  });
});
```

This pattern ensures the dashboard reflects filesystem state without polling, and the approval gate ensures no file is written without human sign-off.

